¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And lay up his words in thine heart.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ7If thou return to the Almighty, thou shalt be built up,¦layout ‚¤textÙ6Thou shalt put away iniquity far from thy tabernacles.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ$Then shalt thou lay up gold as dust,¦layout ‚¤textÙ2And the gold of Ophir as the stones of the brooks.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'Yea, the Almighty shall be thy defence,¦layout ‚¤textÙ%And thou shalt have plenty of silver.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ5For then shalt thou have thy delight in the Almighty,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And shalt lift up thy face unto God.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ<Thou shalt make thy prayer unto him, and he shall hear thee,¦layout ‚¤text¼And thou shalt pay thy vows.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙFThou shalt also decree a thing, and it shall be established unto thee:¦layout ‚¤textÙ(And the light shall shine upon thy ways.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙAWhen men are cast down, then thou shalt say, there is lifting up;¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And he shall save the humble person.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,He shall deliver the island of the innocent:¦layout ‚¤textÙ3And it is delivered by the pureness of thine hands.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse